# Working files / experiments — kept on local disk but never committed.
#
# Anything Bugbite production actually serves should be committed
# individually (and is, for now: logo-light.png, logo-mark.png,
# cat-walking.gif, Animatedlogo.mp4). Working files below stay local
# so the repo doesn't bloat with sources we've already converted
# downstream into the production assets.

# AI-generated frame samples and brand experiments (one-off PNG/JPG
# tests that don't ship anywhere)
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# ezgif.com round-trip artifacts — we use ffmpeg-encoded GIFs instead
# (better frame rate control, smaller output)
ezgif*.gif

# Source videos for derived assets — only the converted output ships
# (e.g. cat-walking.gif is encoded from "Black cat animated logo... .mp4")
Black cat*.mp4
